#!spectest
# mode: run
# adjudicator: ggdef
# doc: migrated from tests/fixtures/dict_callable_get_clone.gg (run_gg pair)
# expect:
#   exit: 0
#   stdout: "2\n11\ndone\n"
#!end
# Regression: Dict[K, Callable].get().unwrap().clone() must not double-free.
#
# Background (security-flagged in TODO 2026-04-28): Dict.get() returns
# Option[V] BY VALUE. After deep-clone work landed `needs_drop=true` for
# Callable, the unwrap result of Dict.get() shared its `env` pointer with
# the Dict slot. The unwrap result got a scope-exit drop registered, which
# called gorget_closure_free on the shared env. The next free (caller's
# clone result OR the Dict's val_drop on its own slot) hit a freed env →
# `free(): double free detected in tcache 2`.
#
# Strings dodge the same shape via CoW (cap=0 views skip free); Callable
# has no view/owner distinction, so it had to be plumbed at the IR level.
from std.collections import Dict

void main():
    Dict[String, Callable[int(int)]] d = Dict[String, Callable[int(int)]]()
    d.put("k", (int x): x + 1)
    Callable[int(int)] g = d.get("k").unwrap().clone()
    print(g(1))           # expected: 2
    print(g(10))          # expected: 11 — confirms env still valid after clone
    print("done")
